From: DotRedstone <dotredstone@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backend: qualify finger before immediate capture

The FINGER_DOWN_SETUP command first raises a short command-completion IRQ.
Waiting for that IRQ alone does not mean that a finger is present. Poll the
trusted application's qualification operation with a cancellation-aware
backoff, then ask CAPTURE to image the finger immediately instead of making it
wait for a second finger-down transition.

This prevents command-completion IRQs from producing a tight stream of empty
captures while preserving the real touch IRQ as the wake-up source.
---
 backend/src/fpc_qtee_client.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/backend/src/fpc_qtee_client.c b/backend/src/fpc_qtee_client.c
index 09fd084..3544145 100644
--- a/backend/src/fpc_qtee_client.c
+++ b/backend/src/fpc_qtee_client.c
@@ -566,12 +566,19 @@ int fpc_qtee_sensor_wait_finger_down(struct fpc_qtee_client *client,
 		int qualification;
 
 		do {
+			if (atomic_load_explicit(&client->cancelled,
+						 memory_order_relaxed)) {
+				ret = -ECANCELED;
+				break;
+			}
 			qualification = fpc_qtee_sensor_command(
 				client, FPC_SENSOR_IRQ_QUALIFICATION, NULL);
 			if (qualification < 0) {
 				ret = qualification;
 				break;
 			}
+			if (qualification == 0)
+				usleep(20000);
 		} while (qualification == 0);
 	}
 	{
@@ -746,11 +753,11 @@ int fpc_qtee_sensor_capture_sequence(struct fpc_qtee_client *client,
 		goto restore;
 	for (unsigned int attempt = 0; attempt < 4; attempt++) {
 		ret = fpc_qtee_sensor_wait_finger_down(
-			client, sysfs_node, 0, timeout_ms);
+			client, sysfs_node, 1, timeout_ms);
 		debug_log("capture finger-down attempt %u: %d\n", attempt, ret);
 		if (ret)
 			break;
-		ret = fpc_qtee_sensor_capture(client, 1, capture_detail);
+		ret = fpc_qtee_sensor_capture(client, 0, capture_detail);
 		debug_log("capture image attempt %u: ret=%d detail=%u\n",
 			  attempt, ret, *capture_detail);
 		if (ret != 1)
